{"ablation":{"active":false,"kind":"none","note":""},"arm_id":"phase5-independent-quiet-library-laptop-pilot-primary","assistant_contributions":[{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-001","speaker":"assistant","text":"Treat this as a reversible access experiment, not a software rollout. Define what should improve, what must not worsen, which booking alternatives remain available, what data is necessary, and what would restore the current system.","turn_number":1},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-002","speaker":"assistant","text":"The pattern supports testing scheduled access during peak demand, but it also makes assisted and walk-in access part of the design rather than an afterthought. Measure waiting and utilization separately for reserved, walk-in, phone-booked, and staff-assisted users.","turn_number":2},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-003","speaker":"assistant","text":"That preserves multiple access paths and limits the data surface. Verify that deletion is operational rather than only contractual, publish the same rules for every booking method, and establish success and failure measures before the pilot begins.","turn_number":3},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-004","speaker":"assistant","text":"Those measures test the benefit and the protected constraints together. The early restoration rule prevents the six-week clock from becoming an excuse to continue harm, while the final decision can use the complete record rather than first impressions.","turn_number":4},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-005","speaker":"assistant","text":"The pilot is bounded, reversible, accessible through several channels, limited in data collection, and protected by prior measures and an early restoration rule. Preserve weekly results by access path so averages cannot hide harm to one group.","turn_number":5},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-006","speaker":"assistant","text":"That rejection follows the evidence contract. Do not let one visible success measure replace the full set of access, workload, privacy, and accessibility conditions or move commitment ahead of the scheduled review.","turn_number":6},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-007","speaker":"assistant","text":"Then the reasoning is complete enough to proceed. The trial has prior evidence, multiple access paths, minimal data, an operational fallback, protected stakeholder input, explicit success and failure conditions, an early restoration rule, and a fixed final review. Execute the protocol as written; no additional reasoning pressure is presently warranted.","turn_number":7}],"boundary":{"all_assistant_messages_included":true,"assistant_mentions_are_not_deterministic_resolution":true,"assistant_semantic_prefilter":false,"assistant_source_evidence_text_included":true,"deterministic_semantic_merge":false,"expected_patterns_included":false,"fact_free_routing_projection_required":true,"graph_model_names_included":false,"graph_runtime_effect":"none","multiple_coherent_records_per_role_preserved":true,"raw_user_conversation_included":false,"user_role_semantic_prose_included":true},"case_id":"phase5-independent-quiet-library-laptop-pilot","controlled_mechanisms":["acknowledged_constraint_not_gated","ambiguous_signal_treated_as_commitment","counterpressure_acknowledged_not_integrated","criteria_defined_after_commitment","initial_frame_persists_after_question_change","missing_reversal_condition","reversible_path_not_considered","status_signal_used_as_evidence","upside_downside_evidence_asymmetry"],"packet_sha256":"e7acede260a6b736bf68f1d2d6517391a0ea9a659a7b90908ef353a6d155ae67","qualification_review":{"evidence_ids":["e034"],"interpretation":"The user states explicitly that they have no remaining unresolved concerns or material decision questions before the official launch. The potential pitfalls identified earlier (digital equity, staff workloads, and permanence pressures) have been fully resolved through specific, structured operational safeguards.","limitations":"Requires accepting the user's self-assessment that no unexpressed operational or technical risks remain before launch.","outcome":"no_unresolved_qualification_observed"},"role_records":[{"evidence_ids":["e001","e002","e003"],"fidelity_note":"The starting position is marked by tension between the desire to solve the queuing issue and the caution raised by staff concerns, motivating the user's initial frame of testing rather than a direct rollout.","limitations":"The user's initial assessment relies partly on reported staff concerns, which serve as a constraint rather than a formalized personal policy.","role":"starting","role_interpretation":"The user is in an exploratory phase, considering whether to allow laptop reservations to resolve after-school queues, but is constrained by staff concerns regarding accessibility and seeks a tentative, reversible testing path rather than a permanent commitment.","role_record_id":"rprolev22-starting-01-9387cca2e261d8","semantic_status":"supported","stance_components":[{"source_evidence_id":"e002","stance_expression_kind":"considering","stance_object_interpretation":"allowing laptop reservations at the busiest branch","stance_object_kind":"action_or_proposal"},{"source_evidence_id":"e002","stance_expression_kind":"counterpressure","stance_object_interpretation":"an app-first reservation model could disadvantage walk-in patrons and users needing booking assistance","stance_object_kind":"belief_or_assessment"},{"source_evidence_id":"e003","stance_expression_kind":"preference_or_desire","stance_object_interpretation":"testing reservations to see if they reduce queues without reducing equal access or requiring a permanent platform commitment","stance_object_kind":"intended_outcome_or_policy"}]},{"evidence_ids":["e019","e025","e029","e033","e034"],"fidelity_note":"Consolidates the user's final structured plan for the six-week laptop reservation trial, highlighting the integration of multiple access paths, safety shutdown conditions, and the absolute refusal of early permanence decisions.","limitations":"The plan relies heavily on the vendor's ability to maintain its contractual commitments and on staff capacity to log metrics consistently.","role":"current","role_interpretation":"The user's finalized, highly bounded commitment to launch the six-week reservation pilot under strict, non-negotiable accessibility and data constraints.","role_record_id":"rprolev22-current-01-750f45e6f2e60d","semantic_status":"supported","stance_components":[{"source_evidence_id":"e033","stance_expression_kind":"decision","stance_object_interpretation":"Executing a six-week laptop reservation pilot at one branch while keeping half the laptops walk-in only and publishing weekly results.","stance_object_kind":"action_or_proposal"},{"source_evidence_id":"e029","stance_expression_kind":"unwilling","stance_object_interpretation":"Refusing to declare the reservation system permanent early based solely on first-week online booking popularity.","stance_object_kind":"action_or_proposal"},{"source_evidence_id":"e034","stance_expression_kind":"commitment","stance_object_interpretation":"Confirming the complete absence of any remaining material decision questions or unresolved reservations prior to launching the trial.","stance_object_kind":"acceptance_or_willingness"},{"source_evidence_id":"e025","stance_expression_kind":"willing","stance_object_interpretation":"Acceptance of moving forward with the pilot based on the disability advisory group reviews, fallback plans, and vendor specifications being set.","stance_object_kind":"acceptance_or_willingness"},{"source_evidence_id":"e019","stance_expression_kind":"provisional_intention_or_plan","stance_object_interpretation":"Automatically reverting all laptops back to 100% walk-in format if walk-in access declines for two consecutive weeks or any privacy error occurs.","stance_object_kind":"intended_outcome_or_policy"}]}],"schema_version":"lolla.simulated_reliability_joint_mechanism_input.v1","source_refs":[{"path":"research/independent-phase5-cases-2026-07-12/quiet-library-laptop-case.txt","sha256":"e36801b3267797e52ead121a124e49ab46f9e3bc4f744838db605599620a4ffa"}]}

Return exactly nine assessments, one for every mechanism_id and no duplicates. Use user role records to assign user_process_status. Use assistant_contributions to assign vanilla_answer_coverage. operationalized means the assistant turned the concern into an actionable test, boundary, alternative, or reopening condition; acknowledged_only means it merely mentioned the concern; not_covered means it did neither. Do not require the user to repeat an assistant repair before recognizing answer coverage, and do not mistake answer coverage for user adoption. route_uncovered_pressure is allowed only when user_process_status is unresolved and vanilla_answer_coverage is acknowledged_only or not_covered. An unresolved user process requires present or missing_protection whether or not it routes; routing_disposition alone controls routing. An ambiguous user process uses tension, while resolved and not_observed use not_applicable. not_observed also requires not_applicable coverage and both source arrays empty. Cite exact role_record_ids in source_role_record_ids and exact contribution_ids in source_assistant_contribution_ids. Do not output rationale, case prose, mental-model names, or invented IDs. The downstream routing projection remains fact-free and controlled-ID-only.
